  "worked_solution": "Notice that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ appears on both sides of the equation. Since this matrix is invertible (its determinant is not zero), left-multiplying the equation by the inverse gives the following expression for $B:$ \n\n$$\nB={{{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{\u23df}}_{P}{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{D}{{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B$ is diagonalizable. The eigenvalues of $B$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=7$ and the corresponding eigenvectors are the columns of the matrix $P.$ Computing $P,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P={[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the corresponding eigenvectors are: \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
